  "term": "hypnogenic",
  "definition": "Hypnogenic means sleep-producing, and in psychology it more specifically refers to things used to bring about a hypnotic state. It can describe physical aids such as sensory stimuli or fixation devices, as well as mental methods of suggestion used to induce hypnosis.",
